# Upstream merges must bring CODE and never touch this repo's RECORD.
#
# This repo and its upstream both run the same daily audit, and both commit the
# generated research files. Upstream rewrites all ~960 rows; so does this repo.
# Git cannot reconcile two independently regenerated data files, so without this
# EVERY `git merge upstream/main` stops on a conflict in data nobody wants from
# the other side.
#
# `merge=ours` keeps this repo's version unconditionally. That is not a
# convenience: data/snapshots/ is an append-only forward record, and a merge that
# could rewrite an already-published snapshot would make its past mutable. A
# record whose past can change proves nothing.
#
# REQUIRES A ONE-TIME LOCAL SETUP -- `merge=ours` names a driver git does not
# ship, and driver definitions live in .git/config, which cannot be committed.
# In every clone, run once:
#
#     git config merge.ours.driver true
#
# Without it git reports `driver ours not found` and falls back to a normal
# conflict. Noisy, but never silent, and never destructive.

data/latest_research.csv     merge=ours
data/previous_research.csv   merge=ours
data/breadth_history.csv     merge=ours
data/snapshots/**            merge=ours

# Generated binary; published as a release asset, never merged.
data/price_panel.npz         binary merge=ours
